      <h2 class="mt-7">The hiring path: three steps, ~five days</h2>
      <ol class="text-muted pl-5">
        <li><strong>Discovery call (30 min, free):</strong> What's draining your week, the two or three highest-leverage moves for the first 30 days, and whether we fit. You leave with a punch list either way. <a href="/booking/">Book it here</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Proposal (within 24 hours):</strong> One page: scope, format, starting deliverables, pricing, mutual NDA. Plain language, no legal padding.</li>
        <li><strong>Sign &amp; start (within 5 business days):</strong> Kickoff call, decision-rights doc, operating rhythm installed in week one. First deliverable lands in days.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2 class="mt-7">The Objections, Answered Straight</h2>
      <p><strong>"Remote can't work for executive support."</strong> The evidence says otherwise: 80% faster team response, 200+ agents onboarded, market entry on three continents, all delivered remotely. Remote-first forces the documentation discipline most in-office EAs never build.</p>
      <p><strong>"I've been burned by VA agencies."</strong> So have most of my clients. The difference is structural: agencies sell junior hours through templates; this is one senior operator with named testimonials, published case studies, and a portfolio of <a href="/portfolio/">real deliverables you can open</a>.</p>
      <p><strong>"The time zones won't line up."</strong> EAT (UTC+3) covers European hours live and US East mornings-to-afternoon. US founders get a pre-staged morning: work moves while you sleep. Ask the Stockholm fintech how it worked.</p>
      <p><strong>"It's risky to give someone this much access."</strong> Mutual NDA, client-owned systems, encrypted storage, written decision rights, monthly terms, no lock-in. You hold the keys at all times.</p>
      <p><strong>"How do I know the quality is real?"</strong> Seven verified Google reviews, including named engagements at Pioneer Outsourcing BPO and Gregory Swarn Enterprises. <a href="/case-studies/">Seven published case studies</a>. <a href="/portfolio/">Live artifacts</a>. Direct references after the discovery call.</p>

      <h2 class="mt-7">What Happens in the First 30 Days</h2>
      <p>Week 1: kickoff, systems audit, decision-rights doc, triage rules live. Week 2: operating cadence installed, including tracker, decision log, and weekly report. Weeks 3–4: I own the highest-leverage items end-to-end and you see the hours-back number move. The metric I report weekly is the one that matters: how much of your time came back.</p>
